## Layer 1: Structure Component Hardening & Sidebar Polish

### Scope Contract
Sanity Studio is defaulting its internal type evaluation to the first overall schema type (`hero`) when processing heavily customized `S.documentTypeList` configurations. Because it loses the original Type Context, it crashes when validating the `sortOrder` ordering array against the `hero` schema. We must harden the component by switching to an explicitly configured `S.documentList()`. We will also fix the duplicate "Homepage" sidebar item caused by a schema ID typo.

### DoD

- [ ] 1.1 — In `sanity/structure.ts`: Refactor `buildCatalogueTree(S, parentId)` to use a pure `S.documentList()` explicitly linked to the catalogue schema. 
  Replace `return S.documentTypeList("catalogueItem")` and its immediate chained properties with this exact robust structure:
  ```typescript
  return S.documentList()
    .id(parentId ? `catalogue-node-${parentId}` : "catalogue-root")
    .title(parentId ? "Sub-Items" : "Catalogue")
    .schemaType("catalogueItem")
    .filter(filter)
    .params(parentId ? { parentId } : {})
    .defaultOrdering([{ field: "sortOrder", direction: "asc" }])
    .initialValueTemplates(
      parentId ? [S.initialValueTemplateItem("catalogueItem-with-parent", { parentId })] : []
    )
    .child((documentId: string) =>
  ```
  *(Leave the `.child(...)` logic untouched aside from connecting it to this modified chain)*
  - Difficulty: 2 - B(sanity/structure.ts): replace documentTypeList with explicitly architected documentList

- [ ] 1.2 — In `sanity/structure.ts`: Scroll to the bottom export. Update the global structure filter array to correctly hide the system-generated Homepage list.
  Change: `!["catalogueItem", "homepage"].includes(item.getId()!)` 
  To: `!["catalogueItem", "homepageData"].includes(item.getId()!)`
  - Difficulty: 1 - E(sanity/structure.ts): filter out duplicate homepage list item

### Verification — Layer 1

- [ ] V1.1 — Open Sanity Studio at `http://localhost:3001/studio`. Verify "Homepage" strictly appears ONCE in the sidebar. Click the "Catalogue" folder. It must securely render the folder nodes without any schema validation or ordering parameter crashes.
  - Difficulty: 1

